WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.660
On a Monday, most people stepping out of an office lift are in tailored clothes.

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:08.770
By Friday, the most common outfit is jeans and a T-shirt.

00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:12.760
A new doctoral thesis asks what happens in between,

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:15.090
and what office workers are really dressing for.

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:19.690
For thirty weeks, we stood in the lift lobbies of six office buildings,

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:23.170
and coded more than two hundred and twelve thousand arrivals.

00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:26.240
Formality fell through the week, not at its end.

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:29.651
Thursday sat sixty-one per cent of the way from Monday to Friday,

00:00:29.851 --> 00:00:31.391
and slid further every ten weeks.

00:00:32.291 --> 00:00:34.041
Thursday had a tell of its own:

00:00:34.241 --> 00:00:36.791
the jacket carried over an arm, rather than worn.

00:00:37.391 --> 00:00:40.681
And Friday dressed down even in buildings with no casual Friday.

00:00:41.781 --> 00:00:45.211
Forty-eight workers then kept dress diaries, linked to their calendars.

00:00:45.711 --> 00:00:50.451
On eighty-three per cent of office days, the outfit matched the day's most formal meeting.

00:00:50.751 --> 00:00:53.201
Only forty-nine per cent matched the day of the week.

00:00:54.101 --> 00:00:58.461
An outfit, the thesis argues, is a forecast of the day's most formal encounter.

00:00:59.361 --> 00:01:04.381
A trial in twenty-four teams gave each weekday a dress band, with meetings booked to match.

00:01:04.681 --> 00:01:06.028
Thursday held its band,

00:01:06.228 --> 00:01:08.038
and Wednesday slipped below its own.

00:01:08.938 --> 00:01:12.258
The School has since adopted the bands for its own staff.

00:01:12.558 --> 00:01:16.528
Its first review, next February, is likely to lower Wednesday's band.

00:01:17.428 --> 00:01:21.168
On a Thursday, the jacket over the arm isn't a lapse from Monday.

00:01:21.468 --> 00:01:24.048
It's kept for the meeting the calendar didn't announce.
